  "raw_text": "l. Agent: Thank you for explaining your ordering routine. How does price change your choice?... User: Thank you. Agent: You're welcome. How does price change your choice? For example, if your McDonald's cheeseburger meal cost two dollars more, what would you do? User: I use the rewards program or whatever so I get discounts and I get points to add to future purchases. It works out pretty well. Agent: That's smart to use the rewards program. So, if your usual McDonald's cheeseburger meal, even with your rewards, cost two dollars more than it typically does, what would you do? Would you still order it, or would you choose something else? User: I mean if it's just like overnight change, $2 more, I probably would, depends on if I had the money to have the $2 extra to afford it, I guess. But I would probably change my order if I didn't have, if I had like a set amount and that wasn't, that $2 extra wasn't going to be able to be covered in my purchase then I would get something else. Agen",
